# Feeds name-conflict resolution table.
#
# Format: <package-directory-name> <feed-that-should-provide-it>
#
# scripts/build_istoreos.py walks the checked-out feeds/ tree after
# 'scripts/feeds update' but before 'scripts/feeds install'. Any package
# directory whose basename matches the first column is moved out of the build
# tree everywhere EXCEPT inside the feed named in the second column. This
# guarantees the designated feed wins while still clearing the same-named copy
# that ships with the upstream (jjm2473) packages/luci/third feeds.
#
# Use "-" as the second column to drop a package from every feed. The package
# is then neither installed nor built. This is how packages that are broken
# with the current kconfig/toolchain, or that nothing selected depends on, are
# kept out of the build entirely.

# Shared proxy engines: helloworld is the single source, so drop the copies
# that the upstream jjm2473 packages feed would otherwise provide.
sing-box helloworld
xray-core helloworld
v2ray-core helloworld
v2ray-geodata helloworld
microsocks helloworld
luci-app-homeproxy helloworld

# PassWall LuCI application comes from the Openwrt-Passwall feed. helloworld
# also ships a copy, which is dropped here.
luci-app-passwall passwall

# Nikki stack comes from the OpenWrt-nikki feed. helloworld mirrors the same
# package names, so its copies are dropped.
luci-app-nikki nikki
nikki nikki
mihomo-meta nikki
# mihomo-meta and mihomo-alpha CONFLICT with each other, and both PROVIDE the
# virtual 'mihomo' symbol. Two mutually conflicting providers make kconfig
# report "recursive dependency detected!". mihomo-meta is the stable variant,
# so drop mihomo-alpha everywhere.
mihomo-alpha -

# OTA: replace the iStoreOS-native luci-app-ota/otahelper with sbwml's copies
# so the updater can be driven by our own gh-pages manifest.
luci-app-ota openwrt_pkgs
otahelper openwrt_pkgs

# openwrt_pkgs mirrors a few packages that the baseline feeds already ship.
# Keep the baseline provider so the standard version wins.
coremark packages
luci-app-adguardhome luci
luci-app-vlmcsd third
vlmcsd third

# luci-app-ssr-plus (helloworld feed) declares several conditional engine
# dependencies (+PACKAGE_luci-app-ssr-plus_INCLUDE_X:y where the engine has arch
# restrictions). That pattern makes kconfig report "recursive dependency
# detected!" for every engine. Nothing we select depends on luci-app-ssr-plus,
# so drop it everywhere. Its engines (chinadns-ng, shadowsocksr-libev, ...) are
# still pulled by luci-app-passwall where needed.
luci-app-ssr-plus -

# luci-app-baidupcs-web (third feed) depends on a 'baidupcs-web' backend that no
# feed ships, which makes the package scanner warn on every build. Drop the
# unused LuCI front-end so the dependency goes away.
luci-app-baidupcs-web -
